cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TUNA: A streamlined quantum chemistry program for atoms and diatomics"
message: "If you use TUNA in your work, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brough
    given-names: Harry
    email: harry.brough@manchester.ac.uk
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, The University of Manchester"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8373-4023"
abstract: >-
  An open-source quantum chemistry program specifically designed for atoms and
  diatomic molecules. Energies, geometry optimisations, vibrational frequencies,
  response properties, coordinate scans and ab initio molecular dynamics are
  available through a command-line interface, with reference implementations of
  density functional theory, many-body perturbation theory and coupled cluster
  theory.
